+# T09: document refusals name the file and mark its row; Issuer ID never merges two issuers
+
+Model: Sonnet 5.5, medium effort, round 1. BASE: edebd9d817e97a9480fda8d6a8bf11714d179731.
+
+## Findings
+- J2-003 (with C2-011, J2-007): the service's single refusal text is now turned into one reader sentence
+  and the named file's row is marked "Ignored" with that sentence beside it. The file name keeps its own case;
+  a 0-byte file reads "empty.txt is empty (0 bytes)."; the decoder text is gone.
+  Limit: the service stops at its first unreadable file, so one refusal still names one file (listing every
+  problem at once needs a service change, which is outside T09's files; not done).
+- J5-004 (with C2-014): `issuerIdFor` (plain.ts). At review time, if the name's usual (cut at 40) ID is 40 long and
+  not hand-typed or carried, the page looks up the latest run under that ID. Same issuer name (letters and digits
+  compared) keeps the usual ID, so repeated runs keep their ID. A different issuer gets the first 31 characters, a hyphen and
+  an 8-hex code from its whole name (40 characters, matches `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}`, the service's rule in
+  `service.py` `_ISSUER`). The slug rule itself is unchanged, so no existing ID moves. An owner run with no
+  recorded name counts as the same issuer. A failed lookup fails the review (no silent merge).
+  C2-014: a help line under Issuer ID states the rule. Transliterating Ø and similar was not done: it would change
+  existing issuers' IDs.
+- `issuerSlug` lives in `web/src/pages/connected/api.ts` (outside my files); I did not change it.
