+### Findings addressed
+- J5-004 / C2-014, ruling L18. Service: `refuse_filed_elsewhere` (submissions.py) refuses an Issuer ID that runs hold
+  under a different issuer name, with the sentence `Issuer ID "x" is already filed under "H", a different issuer from
+  "N". Use another Issuer ID for this issuer.` Names are compared by `issuer_key` (NFKD, lower case, marks dropped, only
+  a-z and 0-9), the same reduction as the page's `issuerKey`. It runs in the summary (`_summarise`) and in `digest`,
+  which Submit's `_record_for` calls before it saves a record, so a hand-typed ID, a carried ID with a changed name and an
+  ID filed between review and Submit all stop; scheduler.py needed no change. An ID is free when no run holds it, when any
+  run under it carries this name or no name (the same issuer re-submitting is accepted), and an ID already shared by two
+  issuers still accepts either of them. An unreadable record file is skipped, as `prior.issuer` skips it (documented
+  fail-open; the rest of the check is not).
+- Page (plain.ts, StartRun.tsx): the holder of every ID built from a name is looked up, not only 40-character ones
+  (review findings 1 and the adversarial finding 1: a cut on a word boundary and a short name that collides). The holder name
+  comes from `/api/issuers/<id>` (`issuer_name`), one request, not `getPriorInputs`; a failed lookup falls back to the usual
+  ID because the service now refuses a clash. The ID is settled before "Carry over from latest run" looks up and locks it,
+  so a different issuer no longer carries another's run and the issuer's own suffixed runs are found. The review sheet says
+  `Issuer ID <id> was used for this run because <usual> is already filed under <holder>, a different issuer.` (a line
+  under the sheet; ReviewSheet.tsx is not mine). A service refusal (summary or Submit) is shown on the Issuer ID field in
+  reader words naming the holder, with a button `Use <suffixed ID>`; a refusal at Submit clears the review and returns to
+  Documents.
+- J2-003 review finding 2 (High): `discardDocument` now reads through the same `readDocuments(draft)` as every other read,
+  so removing one bad file names the next one in a reader sentence and the removed file does not come back as an Ignored row.
+- Review finding 3 (Medium): the document sentence is `X could not be read.` plus a reason only where the service's message
+  states it (a decode failure: "its text could not be decoded."; "not a zip file": "its contents are not a valid zip
+  archive."). The false "not a <ext> file" and the "a xlsx" are gone.
+- Review finding 4: `web/node_modules` removed from the branch (`git rm --cached`); the local symlink stays, untracked.
