+## Round 3
+
+Model: Sonnet 5.5, medium effort (owner instruction: T07 to T10 implementers run on Sonnet at medium effort).
+Base of the round: b0cbffc1. Round-2 reviews (`T09-review-2.md`, `T09-review-2-adversarial.md`) addressed as below.
+
+### Findings addressed
+- Adversarial 1 (Medium): `issuer_key` (submissions.py) and `issuerKey` (plain.ts) now keep Unicode letters and digits:
+  NFKD, lower case, then only `\p{L}`/`\p{N}` (Python: category L or N) kept; marks drop out because they are neither. So
+  "中国银行 Ltd" (`中国银行ltd`) and "中国建设银行 Ltd" (`中国建设银行ltd`) differ and no longer merge. Lower case, not full
+  case folding, is used on both sides so the two stay identical ("ß" and "ø" stay as letters: `straßeholdingsplc`,
+  `ørstedas`; "İ" gives "i"). Same literal cases on both sides, now including Газпром ПАО, Йога-Центр and the two Chinese names.
+  Limit documented in both docstrings: Python and Node carry different Unicode versions (37 recent characters differ), so two
+  names differing only in such a character may compare differently on the page and in the service; the service's answer counts;
+  no table is kept.
+- Standard 1 = adversarial 2 (Medium): `issuerIdRefusal(message, usualHolder)` offers the name's usual ID when it is free or
+  held by the same issuer, and the suffixed ID only when another issuer holds the usual one (or when the refused ID is the
+  usual one). The page looks up the usual ID's holder (`holderOf`) when the refused ID is not the usual one. Tests changed
+  because they pinned the old behaviour: unit test "gives a reader sentence and offers the suffixed ID" in `plain.test.ts` (now
+  "offers the name's usual ID when it is free, not the suffixed one", plus a suffixed-ID case); walk step 2 in
+  `T09/walk-issuer-id.cjs` (expected the suffixed offer `Use ...-[0-9a-f]{8}` and a suffixed taken ID, now `Use
+  eastmoor-synthetic-utilities-plc`).
+- Adversarial 3 (Low): a name with no Latin letters has no usual ID (`issuerIdFor` returns ""); the refusal then offers nothing
+  and says "Otherwise type an Issuer ID of your own for <name>."
+- Adversarial 5 and the standard note (Low): the service sentence is now `Issuer ID "x" is filed under the name "H", not
+  "N". If that is this issuer under another name, type that name; otherwise use another Issuer ID.` The page sentence and the
+  review-sheet note say the same (`Issuer ID x is filed under the name "H". If that is this issuer under another name, type
+  that name. Otherwise ...`; the note: `... was used for this run because <usual> is filed under the name "H". If that is
+  this issuer under another name, type that name.`). "A different issuer" is gone from both. Python tests that matched
+  "already filed under" now match "filed under the name" (same assertions otherwise).
+- Standard 2 (Low): "its text could not be decoded" only for text file types (txt, text, md, csv, tsv, json, jsonl, html, xml,
+  log); a damaged workbook or PDF (the service reads any non-PDF, non-workbook file as UTF-8, `_pages` in model/handoff.py, so
+  it fails with the decoder's text) says only "could not be read." The "not a zip file" reason is also not given for a
+  workbook. `plain.test.ts` now models the real service message (`'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0x9c ...` for
+  holdings.xlsx) instead of "File is not a zip file".
+- Standard 3 (Low): two page-level tests in `ConnectedApp.test.tsx`: a refusal at Submit (refused ID the usual one, and a typed
+  ID with the usual one free) clears the review, returns to Documents, shows the sentence on the Issuer ID field
+  (aria-invalid) with its offer; and the review-sheet note.
+- Standard 4 (Low): the round-2 count above is corrected: round 1's code gives 15 failed, 2 passed (re-measured in a scratch
+  checkout of 46d9d25a with the round-2 test files).
